 said  0.0 uh when you when you  have a season that starts that way  something's wrong with the system  so now we've got at least one the  potential for two which should they uh  a conference champion come from the  power five that wasn't up to snuff but  ultimately that that's all good news i  don't worry so much  about those blowout games when great  teams you know are on the field that  happens it happens in the nfl  uh periodically and it will happen again  in this but  i remember back that georgia oklahoma  game in the rose bowl the overtime  thriller  i say we're going to have more chances  at that because  what will happen over the period of  years as this begins  is there will be more spreading of the  great players the great talent in the  united states  they won't all just go to the top three  places but knowing  that there are more chances to get to  the playoffs uh  maybe closer to home yeah i liken it to  gonzaga  because gonzaga used to be a novelty in  basketball  and you know they would be like oh  that's a cute story gonzaga  now gonzaga is getting some of the top  recruits in the country  and a lot of that is is they got an  opportunity if if the field was  32 as it used to be a long long time ago  you would have a lot of these programs  who would never get this opportunity to  grow their program  indiana being on a national stage with  their football program  i thought i would never see that in my  lifetime coastal carolina  you know they would make the playoffs  and i i like that it gives you an  opportunity to be seen by more people  because we wouldn't have seen the  indiana story this year or coastal  carolina  boise state wouldn't exist you know i  think having that opportunity where you  get to play against the big boys  and you know that opportunity for  players to see  or recruits to see you play i i think  it's a benefit for these smaller schools  that would not be  they would be dwarfed by alabama and  clemson and they may still be  but 